{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/803838-unseelie-versus-shadow-court","id":803838,"title":"Unseelie versus Shadow Court","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-08T10:38:55-08:00","id":803838,"title":"Unseelie versus Shadow Court","content":"So, what with the imminent completion of the C20 kickstarter, I've pulled out my mass of Dreaming books from their hiding place under the basement stairs in an effort to reacquaint myself with the game. One thing in particular has me annoyed from some of the older books. It seems like there was a miscommunication between the authors regarding if the Shadow Court represented anyone who was Unseelie primary or was a separate organization that was specifically the&quot;evil&quot; side of Dreaming (ie - Dreaming's pentex, sabbot,or technocracy ).<br /> <br /> Hell, even in the Shadow Court book, there are sections that one paragraph imply one, and the very next imply the opposite. <br /> <br /> Hopefully this inconsistency will be resolved in C20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:11:33-08:00","id":803914,"title":"","content":"Well the 'official' Shadow Court refers to the Unseelie Court that would rule on Samhain. The unofficial Shadow Court is a secret society of Winter-hungry, human-hating, Seelie-loathing Villains(TM).<br /> <br /> It's the same way that Unseelie refers to an actual Court of changelings but also to changelings whose Unseelie Legacy is dominant, whether or not they consider themselves part of the Unseelie Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:44:09-08:00","id":803943,"title":"","content":"Something Ive thought on for a bit you just reminded me of, if a a member of house Ailil's Seelie legacy becomes dominant, because of a great success, this wont make him suddenly side against his former allies, and help his enemys, just to be somewhat more humane towards captured enemys, and generous with rewards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:54:46-08:00","id":803951,"title":"","content":"I think Seelie and Unseelie have two meanings inside the game:<br /> 1. The original courts of the Fae. Now extinct in most places.<br /> 2. Your personality, i.e., what legacie you are more inclined to behave.<br /> <br /> And there are two political courts nowadays:<br /> 1. The Shining Host, that keeps the Seelie Code and traditions over other things.<br /> 2. The Shadow Court, a political group of kithain that doesn't feel their voices are heard in the main court and keep their own secret agenda, feeling that nowadays kithain have neglected their Unseelie values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:47:52-08:00","id":804017,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they need separate terms for these things, even if just to stop our heads hurting. Summer and Winter Courts, Seelie and Unseelie Legacies. Shadow Court its own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}